you might think of soap as anything that  washes but in chemistry soap actually  has a very specific meaning it refers to  cleanses made from fats and oils reacted  with a strong base usually lye or sodium  hydroxide soaps are the oldest cleanses  and they're natural but they're actually  quite irritating on your skin first off  soaps don't work when they're acidic so  these true soaps have a high pH your  skin is acidic with a low PH so the high  pH of soaps can disturb your skin  secondly they have very skinny straight  structures so they can get into your  skin more easily and stay there which  means you get prolonged irritation if  you see these high up in the ingredient  lists it's probably going to be a more  irritating cleanser so that's why soap  free cleansers were invented they use  gentler surfactants these days a lot of  things that look like bar soaps might  not actually be bar soaps for example  Dove Beauty Bar and Cetaphil gentle  cleansing bar use isothyanates  surfactants so they can drastically cut  down on the amount of real soap and be  formulated at a low PH that make them  much less irritating
 

